WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
The framework is evaluated on two environments.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.501
The first is MiniGrid,

00:00:04.581 --> 00:00:09.280
a gridworld where an agent must reach a fixed goal
behind a locked door;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:15.321
it is used to qualitatively demonstrate the many
inference tasks a single model can perform

00:00:15.401 --> 00:00:18.441
and to compare task-specific validation losses.

00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:24.084
The second is Maze2D, a continuous-control maze
from the MuJoCo-based D4RL benchmark,

00:00:24.164 --> 00:00:29.926
where the authors measure test-time reward over one
thousand rollouts across five seeds,

00:00:30.006 --> 00:00:34.639
comparing Uni-MASK against a feedforward network,
Decision Transformer,

00:00:34.719 --> 00:00:39.950
and their own improved Decision-GPT baseline at
context lengths of five and ten.
